            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0394" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/749.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Arbitrator to
                        the President.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As the Arbitrator named by you under
                    Article 27 of the contract dated June 14th, 1897, between the Republic of
                    Ecuador and the Guayaquil and Quito Railway Company, to settle in conjunction
                    with the Arbitrator named by the President of Ecuador all controversies or
                    disagreements existing between the contracting parties, I have the honor to
                    report that after a month spent in Quito in prolonged conferences and
                    negotiations with the Ecuadorian Arbitrator, we have not been able to agree.* *
                    *</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
